1
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:13,820
Good morning, everyone. This is Jeff Parke, as I have introduced myself many times, and hopefully the name starts to sound familiar.

2
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:20,840
I am the founder of the Cold Ischemia Foundation. I wanted to make this video

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:30,490
to ensure that we all understand why we exist and to send this personal message directly

4
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:37,800
from me. So if you're watching this, kidney disease has probably walked into your life

5
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:47,730
or into the life of someone you love. Maybe you're on dialysis. Maybe you're waiting for the call that just has not come.

6
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:54,950
Maybe you're the care partner, the one driving, scheduling,

7
00:00:55,610 --> 00:01:06,780
filling the pillbox and holding the whole family together. You see, I want to start with what nobody said to me:

8
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:13,220
that I do see you. I truly, deeply,

9
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:19,930
transparently see you. I'm a patient myself.

10
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:25,950
I've shared my journey. I've dealt with the system for almost three decades.

11
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:37,570
I know what the chair is like. I know how the waiting goes. I've waited to have my third transplant for 10 years.

12
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:44,430
I know what it feels like to be handed a pamphlet when what you needed was an answer.

13
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:52,940
Just an answer. A conversation with a social worker or the transplant coordinator. Something you didn't receive.

14
00:01:54,040 --> 00:02:00,240
And I know the moment you realize that nobody's coming to explain it. And like myself,

15
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:06,460
you are left to figure everything out yourself.

16
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:15,680
This is exactly why I wanted to start this foundation, and that is why

17
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:27,690
I decided to make this audio video. So just let me introduce you quickly, very properly.

18
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:32,960
This is the Cold Ischemia Foundation.

19
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:42,330
The background: in medicine, cold ischemia is the time an organ can survive once it's been cut off from what keeps it alive.

20
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:49,410
And we took that name for a reason. We get a lot of questions as to why we did take that route.

21
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:58,090
We have watched the same thing happen to people. Cut off from the answers,

22
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:04,400
cut off from respect, cut off from any real say

23
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:14,780
in their own care, slowly going cold as they become, to simply feel

24
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:21,660
obsolete, very unimportant, and

25
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:31,090
absolutely have no control over what happens to them and their care. Our whole job

26
00:03:32,910 --> 00:03:40,740
of the Cold Ischemia Foundation is to end that cold... interval. Apologies.

27
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:49,690
And here's what that looks like. We have built many free tools you can use tonight:

28
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:58,600
a living donor assessment, for example, a state-by-state directory of transplant centers with direct phone numbers,

29
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:08,180
guides written for care partners. We build the guides and the mentors who have been where you are,

30
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:16,450
and we build the confidence to understand your own body, your own numbers, and your own choices.

31
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:24,210
Because you do have choices. If you remember one sentence

32
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:30,700
from this video, remember that one: you have choices.

33
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:43,560
So why this particular video, and why now? Because every week someone newly diagnosed types "kidney disease" into a search bar

34
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:52,610
and it lands on a page that feels caring and independent. And too often, that page is paid for

35
00:04:53,580 --> 00:05:01,690
by the companies that profit from what happens next. I'm not calling anyone a villain.

36
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:10,320
I'm telling you that you deserve to know who is paying for the voice that is talking to you.

37
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:16,430
Nobody else is going to say it, and so I've made a point.

38
00:05:17,490 --> 00:05:23,490
I made it a mission to make sure that I will be the one

39
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:33,220
saying this, and saying it loudly. Let's just start with the size of

40
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:45,700
kidney disease. 37 million Americans have kidney disease, and the CDC says 87% of the adults who have it

41
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:55,330
do not know. Think about that. They don't know. Most people find out when it's already a crisis.

42
00:05:56,370 --> 00:06:02,410
That's what happened to me. You kind of crash into dialysis.

43
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:09,920
And when it is a crisis, there are two companies, simply two companies, that you're usually

44
00:06:10,850 --> 00:06:21,380
almost always stuck to choose. DaVita and Fresenius treat roughly three in four dialysis patients

45
00:06:21,790 --> 00:06:31,650
in this country. DaVita alone brought in $13.6 billion last year.

46
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:44,460
In 2024, it paid more than $34 million to settle federal kickback allegations without admitting any liability.

47
00:06:45,590 --> 00:06:55,970
Those are allegations. The revenue is not. Meanwhile, only about one patient in seven dialyzes at home.

48
00:06:57,010 --> 00:07:08,400
A 2025 analysis of 72 studies found that seeing a kidney specialist early cut catheter starts by more than half.

49
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:14,920
That's early, before the crisis. That is what prevention looks like,

50
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:24,170
and it does not bill by the treatment. Now here comes the part some people just won't like.

51
00:07:25,050 --> 00:07:31,150
In 2017, researchers in the New England Journal of Medicine looked at the hundred

52
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:43,740
and four largest patient advocacy organizations in America. And 83% took money from drug, device, or biotech companies.

53
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:52,010
Only, only one of the hundred and four

54
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:59,090
said plainly that it did not. Chew on that, please.

55
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:09,020
Kidney care is no different. The American Kidney Fund has been reported to draw roughly 80% of its donor base from DaVita and Fresenius.

56
00:08:09,930 --> 00:08:16,920
It denies steering patients, and the Justice Department declined to join the whistleblower suit.

57
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:29,360
The National Kidney Foundation's corporate membership lists Boehringer Ingelheim, Novo Nordisk, and Vertex. The American Association of Kidney Patients

58
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:37,970
lists DaVita, Fresenius, and Amgen. Dialysis Patient Citizens was founded with an educational grant

59
00:08:38,670 --> 00:08:49,720
from DaVita. Now, none of that is illegal. Taking industry money is legal and common, and some of these groups do real work.

60
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:57,630
I'm not telling you what to think about any of them. I'm telling you to look at the table

61
00:08:58,770 --> 00:09:09,820
in this video. Now look at us, the Cold Ischemia Foundation. No donations, no funding, gifts, grants, or sponsorships from

62
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:20,310
drugmakers, device makers, dialysis companies, insurers, hospital systems, or any advocacy group they fund.

63
00:09:21,090 --> 00:09:27,380
We charge fees only for services you ask for, at posted rates,

64
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:37,580
and a fee never buys influence. No drugmaker, dialysis company, insurer, or hospital system has a seat

65
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:45,210
on our up-and-coming board. Ask any organization five questions.

66
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:54,140
Who pays you? Who governs you? Who shapes your message? What can't you say?

67
00:09:55,280 --> 00:10:06,800
And who do you answer to? Our answers are simple. Patients and care partners. That's all. And because we have no sponsor to protect,

68
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:14,010
we can name every institution. Independence is not a slogan.

69
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:19,790
It is a structure, and structure builds things.

70
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:32,710
Free toolkits with no paywall, a weekly investigation called the Inside Files, a public scorecard of how Congress acts on transplant and kidney care,

71
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:40,460
formal demand letters to the agencies that run this system.

72
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:49,460
And what is really happening: in 2024, 3,743 people were removed

73
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:58,210
from the kidney waiting list because they died. 29% of the kidneys recovered that year were never transplanted.

74
00:11:00,070 --> 00:11:06,080
Those are not numbers. Those are people. These are real people

75
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:16,040
who died, gave their lives to a system that has betrayed them and let them down,

76
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:23,140
and we will continue to keep saying this very loudly.

77
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:36,610
People, we know, we understand, if you're listening and you're part of an advocacy organization, we get it. You're just going to say, "I'm making accusations that we're just doing this to

78
00:11:36,890 --> 00:11:47,070
create a rift, trying to tear apart whatever bridges that you may think we have been creating.

79
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:55,680
But that's your opinion. But the facts don't lie. And we have the facts, and we share them.

80
00:11:57,330 --> 00:12:08,750
So here's what I'm asking. Don't take my word for it. Not mine, not theirs. Read their Form 990s. Find their sponsor page. Read the board list.

81
00:12:09,050 --> 00:12:18,690
Ask what they have ever said against the people who fund them. We built a free Advocacy Assessment that walks you through it.

82
00:12:20,290 --> 00:12:26,820
Then come with us. Use the tools. Send this to a care partner who is exhausted tonight.

83
00:12:27,590 --> 00:12:35,430
Volunteer. Tell us where the system has failed you, because your experience is evidence.

84
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:42,300
We need people to start using their voices. We get it.

85
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:49,430
We fear retaliation. It happens. Patients get blacklisted. We understand it.

86
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:56,640
But if we can just continue to try and build a unified front,

87
00:12:57,480 --> 00:13:08,720
maybe we can get through to people. And we started this foundation because we were tired of waiting for somebody else to do it.

88
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:16,670
We're not asking for permission. We're building it in the open, with nobody

89
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:23,320
to protect but you, folks. You have choices.

90
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:30,330
And always know you have choices, and you're never alone.

91
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:42,270
Think about it. Share this. Check us out. Just sign up for our free information, and you will see where we are different.

92
00:13:43,310 --> 00:13:50,890
And we are what the future looks like for true patient-centered care.

93
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:52,260
Thank you.
